      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX 3 Image vs Klein\n\nThe same image and the same instruction through both FLUX 3 models, side by side, so you can see what the cheaper, faster Klein gives up on your kind of edit before committing a batch to either.\n\n**Anything Everywhere** (Use Everywhere) carries the loaded image to both models without a wire each. Its input filter is `^input_image$`, so it only fills each node's first reference socket \u2014 never the empty `input_image_2` that appears below it, and never the comparer. Add a third model node and it is fed automatically.\n\n**Fast Groups Bypasser** (rgthree) has one toggle per model group. Switch one off to stop paying for it; a bypassed model passes the source image straight through, so the comparer then shows *source vs the other model*.\n\n**Image Comparer**: `image_a` is FLUX 3 Image, `image_b` is Klein. Two **Display Any** nodes show how each model rewrote the instruction \u2014 Klein's upsampler writes a full scene caption.\n\nKlein's `seed` is fixed at 42; FLUX 3 Image has no seed, only the unsent `variation`.\n\n### Needs\n[rgthree-comfy](https://github.com/rgthree/rgthree-comfy) and [Use Everywhere](https://github.com/chrisgoringe/cg-use-everywhere). **Manager \u2192 Install Missing Custom Nodes** finds both if the graph loads with red nodes. If Use Everywhere is missing, the model nodes get no image and run as **text-to-image** \u2014 install it before you queue.\n\n## The prompt lives in one node\n\nThe **Shared Prompt** node feeds every FLUX 3 `prompt` in this graph, so there is one\nplace to edit it. It emits a plain string, **not** a list, so each node it feeds still runs once."
      ],
      "title": "Read me",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
